{
  "verdict": "request_changes",
  "summary": "The prior findings are addressed in the supplied plan, but three implementation-plan issues remain.",
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Task 8: implementation review transition; Task 12: PR sequence",
      "issue": "[P2] Task 8 requires the authoritative PR round before publishing the PR, while Task 12 requires that round against the published exact PR head. Both sequences cannot be followed.",
      "suggestion": "Make Task 8 use Task 12ΓÇÖs sequence: finish the live gate and local review, publish the ready PR, qualify CI, then review the exact PR head."
    },
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Task 9: Bridge retry cache and engine regressions",
      "issue": "[P2] The cache plan names the prompt digest but does not explicitly bind expected_thread_id to a key. It also does not test replay of an earlier key after a later turn, and its example changes the replayed response by adding `replayed: True`. These leave exact-response replay and different-content conflict insufficiently specified.",
      "suggestion": "Fingerprint every request field after checking the instance ID. Look up an exact retry before validating the current thread for a new turn, return the stored response unchanged, and test changed expected_thread_id and delayed replay after continuation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "important",
      "location": "Task 1 configuration tests; Task 2 MCP artifact-read tests",
      "issue": "[P2] Task 1 requires passing CLI/GitSource/Store/Core entry-path tests before those entry paths are implemented in Tasks 2ΓÇô6. Task 2 likewise requires actual MCP discovery and EOF reads before the server is implemented in Task 6. The stated focused green gates cannot be met in task order.",
      "suggestion": "Keep contract and direct-source tests in their current tasks. Place each entry-path test in the task that creates that entry path, and run the actual MCP artifact tests after Task 6."
    }
  ]
}
